            "number": "01",
            "title": "The Meeting",
            "body": "Harin and Zach met in 2011, at the University of Houston College of Pharmacy, not as business partners, and not yet as anything resembling founders, but as two students in the same pharmacy fraternity, Phi Delta Chi. Both went on to serve as chapter president: Harin in 2012, Zach in 2013."
          }
        },
        "cred_2": {
          "type": "cred",
          "settings": {
            "number": "02",
            "title": "Two Careers",
            "body": "Zach spent the next ten-plus years in community pharmacy, building expertise in over-the-counter products, including the dermatological aisle, and every overpriced bottle in it that promised more than it delivered. Harin moved through long-term care, specialty pharmacy, infusion, and compounding, learning to formulate to a standard with no room for a claim that turned out to be almost true."
          }
        },
        "cred_3": {
          "type": "cred",
          "settings": {
            "number": "03",
            "title": "The Conversation",
            "body": "Their careers came back together when Zach took a position at The Chemist Pharmacy, Harin's pharmacy. Working alongside each other again, they did what old fraternity brothers tend to do: started comparing the decade they'd just spent apart, and found a strange amount of overlap."
          }
        },
        "cred_4": {
          "type": "cred",
          "settings": {
            "number": "04",
            "title": "What Their Wives Actually Wanted",
            "body": "Both married to accountants. Both raising two kids. And both married to women who had spent real money on dermatological products they didn't fully trust and didn't think were worth what they cost. Neither wife was asking for a miracle, they wanted skincare formulated by someone who understood what they were doing, not just someone skilled at selling it."
          }
        },
        "cred_5": {
          "type": "cred",
          "settings": {
            "number": "05",
            "title": "The Bench",
            "body": "So Harin and Zach did the thing they'd spent over a decade training to do, applying the same formulation standards they'd apply to anything touching a prescription pad, building products for their wives specifically. Their wives loved what came out of it. That was the moment the idea stopped being personal and started becoming Chemistrie."
          }
        },
        "cred_6": {
          "type": "cred",
          "settings": {
            "number": "06",
            "title": "Why Chemistrie",
            "body": "Harin and Zach decided the same standard that worked for two women shouldn't stay limited to two women. “We didn't set out to build a skincare brand. We set out to make something our wives could actually trust. Everything else followed from that.” (Harin & Zach)"
          }
        }
      },
